<title>VENEZUELA: CANTV to invest $21 mln on public phones in 1997.</title>
<headline>CANTV to invest $21 mln on public phones in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's national telephone company CANTV said Tuesday it planned to invest $21 million in 1997 to expand its public and rural telephone services.</p>
<p>CANTV said the rural program would concentrate on areas with significant oil, tourism or mining activities, remote areas and border areas.</p>
<p>Government officials have criticized the GTE Corp run company for failing to meet its obligations to install lines in rural areas.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
